    "body": "Rockwell Automation has agreed to buy AGILOX, an Austrian maker of driverless forklifts, from private equity firm Carlyle. Rockwell says the deal would more than double its autonomous mobile robot (AMR) business.\nWhat’s Related\nThe companies announced the agreement on Wednesday. Carlyle took a majority stake in AGILOX in 2021.\nRockwell expects the deal to close in the quarter ending March 31, subject to regulatory approval and other closing conditions. AGILOX would join Rockwell’s Intelligent Devices segment.\nForklifts meet flatbeds\nThe big draw for Rockwell is how AGILOX fits with OTTO, the AMR line it added when it bought Clearpath Robotics in 2023. AGILOX makes forklift robots that move pallets. OTTO is best known for its flatbed robots and already sells a driverless forklift. The deal would give Rockwell more models for moving pallets.\nThere’s a geographic fit too. OTTO is strongest in North America, while AGILOX has an established base in Europe. AGILOX also gets a door into Rockwell’s customers in consumer packaged goods and life sciences.\n“Combining AGILOX and OTTO technologies creates a best-in-class technology platform,” said Blake Moret, Rockwell’s chairman and CEO.\nHe added that the deal “doesn’t just combine strengths; it amplifies innovation and delivers breakthrough value for our customers.”\nWho is AGILOX?\nFounded in 2017 and based in Neukirchen bei Lambach, Austria, AGILOX has deployed more than 2,500 AMRs for customers in automotive , third-party logistics , food and beverage , and pharmaceuticals . It has more than 250 employees and subsidiaries in Europe, the U.S. and China .\nCarlyle says AGILOX has more than 400 customers worldwide and works with more than 40 partners across more than 35 countries. The firm also says AGILOX’s revenue has quadrupled since its 2021 investment.\nAGILOX co-CEOs and co-founders Dirk Erlacher and David Niedermaier said the deal gives the company room to grow.\n“For AGILOX, joining Rockwell Automation represents a transformational step forward,” they said. “This gives AGILOX the scale and market reach that we couldn’t build on our own.”",
